                "event": "Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Indianapolis IN",
                "headline": "Flood Warning issued August 29 at 5:29PM CDT until August 30 at 9:10AM CDT by NWS Indianapolis IN",
                "description": "...The Flood Warning continues for the following river in Illinois...\nIndiana...\n\nWabash River at Hutsonville to Vincennes\n\n.Minor flooding continues on the Wabash River from Hutsonville down\nto Vincennes. The river has crested. Flooding should come to an end\non the Wabash over the weekend.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Vincennes.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 17.0 feet, Considerable agricultural flooding extends\nfrom just north of the junction of Illinois 33 with Business 50 to\nthe St. Francesville, Illinois area.  River Road from Lincoln\nMemorial Bridge to Billett Rd is impassable.  Extensive seep water\nforms behind Illinois levees extending from Russellville to U.S.\nHighway 50.  Flooding of agricultural land begins in Knox County\nIndiana west of the railroad extending for the Oaktown area to the\nnorth side of Vincennes.  Extensive flooding of Small Creek.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 4:45 PM CDT /5:45 PM EDT/ Saturday the stage was 16.8 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 4:45 PM CDT /5:45 PM EDT/ Saturday was 17.8 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\nthis evening and continue falling to 4.4 feet Tuesday, September\n08.\n- Flood stage is 16.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Sunday morning at 915 AM CDT /1015\nAM EDT/.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
